# Anti-Patterns and Verification

## General software and browser work

- Keep components maintainable and focused; refactor large files when beneficial without changing unrelated code.
- Do not hardcode server-controlled metadata in client components.
- Avoid unintended hydration mismatches and unnecessary scroll listeners, paint-intensive filters and dependency growth.
- Prefer CSS where it fulfills the interaction contract; use client-side JS or 3D only where needed for real perspective/occlusion, deterministic reversible progress or accessibility.
- Do not break `position: sticky` with unexpected ancestor clipping/overflow. If clipping is necessary, test actual sticky behavior.
- After code changes run the applicable typecheck/lint/build/tests **when the environment supports them** and report any unrun checks. A passing build is not a visual acceptance.
- Mobile acceptance includes real-device checks (Android/Samsung Internet and iOS Safari where specified), reverse/fast scrolling, small viewport, reduced-motion, navigation and keyboard. Never claim device testing from desktop emulation.

## Genezisi studio homepage only

- Follow `docs/infinite-website/NORTH_STAR_v1.2.md`. Do not force effects, dashboards, or a full AI story ahead of the current approved gate.
- No unverified live email/calendar/CRM actions. Preserve links and independent service identities.
- No direct production merge/deployment without founder consent.

## Digital business card only

- Preserve the existing card product without unnecessary new backend dependencies.
- For card print/export, use a dedicated tested print layout and appropriate `@media print`/`@page` dimensions (including 3.5in × 2in where the product requires them). **Do not apply business-card print dimensions globally to the studio homepage**.
